## Questions I want to keep exploring

When do multiple decision centres strengthen governance?

When do they create confusion or conflict?

How does legal recognition shape the effectiveness of polycentric governance?

Can polycentric governance function effectively when authority is distributed unequally across legal systems?

---

## My current reflection

Ostrom encourages me to see governance complexity not simply as a problem, but as a potential resource.

However, my fieldwork also suggests that complexity alone does not guarantee effective governance.

Whether polycentric arrangements succeed depends on how different legal orders, institutions, and actors recognise one another and negotiate authority within the landscape.

